To effectively manage an agency using AERO-GUARD, your Agency Portal should focus on four pillars: Compliance (Core Value), Operational Efficiency, Financial Health, and Client Experience.

Because AERO-GUARD is a compliance-focused tool, you should prioritize KPIs that demonstrate the "cost of non-compliance" to your clients.


1. Compliance & Risk KPIs (The "AERO-GUARD" Value)
These metrics prove the value of your software to corporate clients by showing how many potential errors or costly violations were prevented.


•	Policy Compliance Rate: The percentage of bookings that adhere to corporate travel policies. 


o	Formula: $(\text{Compliant Bookings} \div \text{Total Bookings}) \times 100$

•	Leakage Rate: The volume of bookings made outside the approved system (e.g., direct with airlines). High leakage means lost data and lack of duty-of-care coverage.

•	ADM Avoidance (Penalty Savings): The number of potential Airline Debit Memos (ADMs) blocked by your system’s pre-ticketing validation.

•	Safety/Duty of Care Coverage: The percentage of bookings with complete traveler profiles (e.g., emergency contacts, passport details, visa info). 

2. Operational Efficiency KPIs
These metrics measure how well your agency staff and the AERO-GUARD system are working together to save time. 


•	First-Time Right Rate: The percentage of bookings that pass compliance validation on the first attempt without needing manual helpdesk intervention.

•	Helpdesk Resolution Time (ART): The average time taken to resolve a PNR flagged for manual review by your team.

•	Average Booking Lead Time: Tracking how far in advance trips are booked. Lower lead times often correlate with higher costs; this allows you to advise clients to book earlier. 

•	Change & Cancellation Rate: Frequency of itinerary changes. A spike here can indicate unclear project timelines or the need for more flexible booking policies. 

3. Financial & Revenue KPIs
Use these to show the agency’s profitability and the ROI you generate for the client.


•	Total Savings from Negotiated Rates: The amount saved by the client by using preferred vendors or corporate discounts, tracked through your platform. 

•	Cost Per Booking: Total operational cost (labor + system fees) divided by the number of processed bookings.

•	Average Booking Value (ABV): Average revenue generated per reservation. 

•	Booking Volume: Total reservations processed over a specific period (daily, weekly, monthly). 

4. Client Experience KPIs
These ensure your agency—and your software—is meeting the needs of the actual travelers.


•	Traveler Satisfaction Score (CSAT): Post-trip survey results regarding the booking experience. 

•	Booking Tool Adoption Rate: The percentage of employees utilizing your authorized booking flow versus alternative, unmanaged methods. 

