Technical Requirements Document: AERO-GUARD MVP
Version: 1.0

Date: August 7, 2026

Project Owner: Soviet George Paradzai

Objective: Develop a B2B travel compliance ecosystem to automate GDS quality control and improve agency operational efficiency.


1. Project Overview
AERO-GUARD is a three-tier compliance platform designed to integrate with Global Distribution Systems (GDS). It aims to reduce Airline Debit Memos (ADMs) and manual processing errors by providing real-time PNR validation, an escalation helpdesk, and an analytical dashboard for management.


2. System Architecture
The system shall consist of three interconnected modules:


1.	AERO-GUARD Smart Button (Client-side): A GDS-embedded widget (HTML5/JS plugin) for real-time PNR scanning.

2.	Central API Server (Backend): A RESTful middleware (Node.js/Python) handling validation logic, user authentication, and data persistence.

3.	Agency Portal (Web Application): A React/Vue-based dashboard for performance analytics and administrative settings.

3. Functional Requirements
3.1. Smart Button (The "Scanner")
•	Trigger: Manual click or automatic intercept upon ET (End Transaction) entry.

•	Data Capture: Capability to parse PNR data (segments, SSRs, OSI, passenger details) from the GDS DOM/API.

•	Validation Engine: Comparison of current PNR against a JSON-based Rule Schema (e.g., Is the ticket time limit set? Is passport data present?).

•	Feedback: Real-time UI overlay indicating "Compliant" (Green) or "Flagged" (Red) with specific error codes.

3.2. Central Server (The "Brain")
•	Authentication: OAuth 2.0 / JWT for secure communication between the Plugin, Portal, and Server.

•	Validation Logic: A modular rules engine allowing admins to toggle rules per client/corporate account.

•	Persistence: PostgreSQL database to store PNR history, audit logs, and compliance status.

•	Webhooks: Asynchronous triggers to notify the Helpdesk module upon critical PNR flags.

3.3. Agency Portal (The "Control Tower")
•	Dashboard: Real-time widgets for:


o	Compliance Rate: Percentage of valid vs. non-compliant PNRs.

o	ADM Savings: Estimated financial impact of prevented errors.

o	Active Queue: List of PNRs awaiting manual helpdesk resolution.

•	Admin Settings: CRUD interface for managing corporate policy rules (e.g., adding a new restricted airline).

4. Technical Stack Recommendations
•	Frontend: React.js or Next.js (for the Portal); Vanilla JS/TypeScript (for the GDS Plugin).

•	Backend: Node.js (Express) or Python (FastAPI).

•	Database: PostgreSQL (Relational data) + Redis (for caching frequent validation rules).

•	Hosting: AWS or Google Cloud (Compute Engine + Managed Database).

•	API Security: HTTPS/TLS 1.3, API Key rotation, and CORS policy enforcement.

5. Non-Functional Requirements
•	Latency: PNR validation must return results within < 2 seconds of the request.

•	Security: Data must be encrypted at rest (AES-256) and in transit. PII (Passport/Contact details) must be masked in logs.

•	Compatibility: Must be compatible with modern Chromium-based browsers (for web-based GDS like Smartpoint/Sabre Red 360).

•	Scalability: API must support concurrent requests from 50+ concurrent agents.

6. Deliverables & Timeline
Milestone	Timeline	Key Output
Phase 1: Core Engine	Weeks 1–4	API endpoints and basic PNR validation logic.
Phase 2: Ops Module	Weeks 5–8	Helpdesk dashboard and status update webhooks.
Phase 3: Analytics	Weeks 9–12	Agency Portal dashboard and Beta deployment.
Instructions for Developers
•	API Documentation: Provide Swagger/OpenAPI documentation upon initiation.

•	Communication: Weekly syncs via MS Teams/Zoom; code repository access via GitHub/GitLab.

•	Compliance: Adhere to IATA data privacy standards regarding passenger information.



